## 1. Problem and facts

**Grounding:**

- **~1 AMQP connection per compute node** (`hpcperfstatsd`); classic queues OOM under this fanout — **keep quorum** (`default_queue_type = quorum` on broker).
- **32 MiB soft merge cap already in tree:** `STATS_BUFFER_RMQ_SOFT_MAX_BYTES` in `monitor/src/stats_buffer.h` — no further payload-size code in this plan.
- **Incident class:** mass `heartbeat_send_error,closed`, handshake timeouts, broker host load when **~2000 nodes reconnect together** after broker stress.
- **Current monitor reconnect** (`stats_buffer_rmq.c`): fixed delay `max(2s, min(send_freq, 30s))`, **no jitter**, **no exponential growth**; backoff resets on first successful publish.
- **Current queue setup:** **non-passive** `queue.declare` + bind on every reconnect from every host (`passive=0` in `amqp_queue_declare`).
- **Post-outage drain:** `ring_buffer_resend_limited` may send up to **64** merged batches per libev tick (`MONITOR_RESEND_MAX_BATCHES_PER_CALL`), 12–25 ms runtime budget — can hammer quorum right as broker recovers.
- **10s AMQP I/O timer** (`monitor.c`) already services heartbeats between publishes — keep it.

**Affected layers:** `monitor/src/stats_buffer_rmq.c`, `monitor/src/monitor_daemon.c`, `monitor/tests/*`, `monitor-rabbitmq-integration-required.mdc`.

